$ Classical simply-supported square plate under uniaxial in-plane
$ compression. SOL 105 linear buckling.
$
$ Geometry: a = b = 1, t = 0.01. Material E = 210e9, nu = 0.3.
$ Reference (Timoshenko & Gere, Theory of Elastic Stability, Ch. 9):
$     sigma_cr = 4 * pi^2 * E * t^2 / (12 * (1 - nu^2) * b^2)
$              ~= 7.591e7 Pa
$ The applied edge load resolves to a uniform sigma_x = 1 Pa, so the SOL
$ 105 eigenvalue equals sigma_cr directly.
$
$ Mesh 5x5 = 25 CQUAD4 over the unit square, 6x6 = 36 nodes.
$ BCs:
$   - All four edges: Uz = 0 (simply supported, plate normal is global Z)
$   - Left edge (x=0): Ux = 0 (anchor for compression)
$   - Node 1 (origin): Uy = 0 (anchor for in-plane Y translation)
$ Loading: uniform compressive resultant 0.01 N applied on the right edge
$ (x=1), distributed by consistent nodal forces (0.001 at corners,
$ 0.002 at interior nodes).
$
SOL 105
CEND
TITLE = Classical SS square plate, uniaxial compression buckling
SUBCASE 1
  LABEL = Static preload (unit uniaxial compression)
  SPC = 1
  LOAD = 1
$ The preload field is the part of this SOL 105 case that both solvers agree
$ is well-posed, so it is requested and used as the parity target for this row.
$ See validation/README.md, "Tabulated commercial-solver values".
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
SUBCASE 2
  LABEL = Buckling eigenvalue
  STATSUB = 1
  METHOD  = 1
BEGIN BULK
$ ---- buckling eigenvalue extraction: subspace inverse iteration ----
$ EIGB / INV is more robust than EIGRL on the reference solver build for
$ small SOL 105 decks. Range [0, 1e9] brackets sigma_cr ~= 7.6e7 Pa.
EIGB, 1, INV, 0.0, 1.0E9, 4
$ ---- small drilling-DOF stiffness avoids near-singular Rz mechanisms ----
PARAM, K6ROT, 100.0
$ ---- material and property ----
MAT1, 1, 2.1+11, , 0.3
PSHELL, 1, 1, 0.01, 1
$ ---- grids: 6x6 on a 1.0 x 1.0 plate, dz = 0 ----
$ Node ID = 6*j + i + 1 ; i, j in 0..5 ; x = 0.2 i, y = 0.2 j.
GRID,  1, , 0.0, 0.0, 0.0
GRID,  2, , 0.2, 0.0, 0.0
GRID,  3, , 0.4, 0.0, 0.0
GRID,  4, , 0.6, 0.0, 0.0
GRID,  5, , 0.8, 0.0, 0.0
GRID,  6, , 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
GRID,  7, , 0.0, 0.2, 0.0
GRID,  8, , 0.2, 0.2, 0.0
GRID,  9, , 0.4, 0.2, 0.0
GRID, 10, , 0.6, 0.2, 0.0
GRID, 11, , 0.8, 0.2, 0.0
GRID, 12, , 1.0, 0.2, 0.0
GRID, 13, , 0.0, 0.4, 0.0
GRID, 14, , 0.2, 0.4, 0.0
GRID, 15, , 0.4, 0.4, 0.0
GRID, 16, , 0.6, 0.4, 0.0
GRID, 17, , 0.8, 0.4, 0.0
GRID, 18, , 1.0, 0.4, 0.0
GRID, 19, , 0.0, 0.6, 0.0
GRID, 20, , 0.2, 0.6, 0.0
GRID, 21, , 0.4, 0.6, 0.0
GRID, 22, , 0.6, 0.6, 0.0
GRID, 23, , 0.8, 0.6, 0.0
GRID, 24, , 1.0, 0.6, 0.0
GRID, 25, , 0.0, 0.8, 0.0
GRID, 26, , 0.2, 0.8, 0.0
GRID, 27, , 0.4, 0.8, 0.0
GRID, 28, , 0.6, 0.8, 0.0
GRID, 29, , 0.8, 0.8, 0.0
GRID, 30, , 1.0, 0.8, 0.0
GRID, 31, , 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
GRID, 32, , 0.2, 1.0, 0.0
GRID, 33, , 0.4, 1.0, 0.0
GRID, 34, , 0.6, 1.0, 0.0
GRID, 35, , 0.8, 1.0, 0.0
GRID, 36, , 1.0, 1.0, 0.0
$ ---- elements (5x5 grid) ----
CQUAD4,  1, 1,  1,  2,  8,  7
CQUAD4,  2, 1,  2,  3,  9,  8
CQUAD4,  3, 1,  3,  4, 10,  9
CQUAD4,  4, 1,  4,  5, 11, 10
CQUAD4,  5, 1,  5,  6, 12, 11
CQUAD4,  6, 1,  7,  8, 14, 13
CQUAD4,  7, 1,  8,  9, 15, 14
CQUAD4,  8, 1,  9, 10, 16, 15
CQUAD4,  9, 1, 10, 11, 17, 16
CQUAD4, 10, 1, 11, 12, 18, 17
CQUAD4, 11, 1, 13, 14, 20, 19
CQUAD4, 12, 1, 14, 15, 21, 20
CQUAD4, 13, 1, 15, 16, 22, 21
CQUAD4, 14, 1, 16, 17, 23, 22
CQUAD4, 15, 1, 17, 18, 24, 23
CQUAD4, 16, 1, 19, 20, 26, 25
CQUAD4, 17, 1, 20, 21, 27, 26
CQUAD4, 18, 1, 21, 22, 28, 27
CQUAD4, 19, 1, 22, 23, 29, 28
CQUAD4, 20, 1, 23, 24, 30, 29
CQUAD4, 21, 1, 25, 26, 32, 31
CQUAD4, 22, 1, 26, 27, 33, 32
CQUAD4, 23, 1, 27, 28, 34, 33
CQUAD4, 24, 1, 28, 29, 35, 34
CQUAD4, 25, 1, 29, 30, 36, 35
$ ---- BCs ----
$ Simply-supported on all 4 edges: Uz = 0
$ bottom (y=0): nodes 1-6
SPC1, 1, 3, 1, THRU, 6
$ top (y=1): nodes 31-36
SPC1, 1, 3, 31, THRU, 36
$ left (x=0): nodes 1, 7, 13, 19, 25, 31
SPC1, 1, 3, 1
SPC1, 1, 3, 7
SPC1, 1, 3, 13
SPC1, 1, 3, 19
SPC1, 1, 3, 25
SPC1, 1, 3, 31
$ right (x=1): nodes 6, 12, 18, 24, 30, 36
SPC1, 1, 3, 6
SPC1, 1, 3, 12
SPC1, 1, 3, 18
SPC1, 1, 3, 24
SPC1, 1, 3, 30
SPC1, 1, 3, 36
$ Anchor left edge in X to take the compressive reaction
SPC1, 1, 1, 1
SPC1, 1, 1, 7
SPC1, 1, 1, 13
SPC1, 1, 1, 19
SPC1, 1, 1, 25
SPC1, 1, 1, 31
$ Anchor a single Y at the origin to remove rigid body Y
SPC1, 1, 2, 1
$ ---- loads: compression on x = 1 edge, total = 0.01 N in -X ----
$ corner nodes (6 and 36): 0.001 each ; interior (12, 18, 24, 30): 0.002
FORCE, 1,  6, , 0.001, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
FORCE, 1, 12, , 0.002, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
FORCE, 1, 18, , 0.002, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
FORCE, 1, 24, , 0.002, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
FORCE, 1, 30, , 0.002, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
FORCE, 1, 36, , 0.001, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
ENDDATA
